| `test_quality.realness.roots` | list of strings | `["tests/e2e"]` in keel and in a generated project; absent, the same value, which its reader reports as `[using default] test_quality.realness.roots = ["tests/e2e"]` | a non-empty list of relative POSIX directories, no empty, `.` or `..` part | `tests/realness.py` (`policy`, `test_files`), called by `tests/integration/test_realness_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `test_quality.realness.roots` row | Moves which directories the realness gate reads test functions from, found as the assertion-quality gate finds them, and fails one whose tier is `mock`. Each configured root must exist and yield at least one test file, and a scan over zero test functions fails. A value the loader refuses raises `ConfigError` naming this key. | a pytest selection: `make test` still runs every test under `tests` | always |
